# Shared exclude list, auto-discovered via `bca.toml`'s
# `exclude_from = ".bcaignore"`. Mirrors the deny-set the self-scan
# workflow and the local baseline refresh both walk. Keep this file and
# `.bca-baseline.toml` in sync — the baseline keys are sensitive to
# which files the walker visits.
#
# Patterns use the `./`-prefix convention. The walker re-anchors every
# seed to that form (#488), so these match the same files regardless of
# whether the root was spelled `.`, `$PWD`, or a manifest-resolved
# absolute path.
#
# Blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is `#`
# are skipped (`.gitignore`-style).

./tree-sitter-*/**
./tests/**
./**/tests/**
./**/*_tests.rs
# Same rationale as `./**/*_tests.rs`, different naming: `test_support.rs`
# is a `#[cfg(test)]`-only module of helpers shared across the per-metric
# test modules (#1066). It is not a sibling unit-test file, so the
# `*_tests.rs` glob does not reach it, and none of it ships.
./src/test_support.rs
./enums/**
./.opencode/**
./target/**
./big-code-analysis-book/**
./docs/**
./packaging/**
./utils/**
./xtask/**
# Dev tooling, same treatment as ./xtask/**: the benchmark harness
# (#1068) ships nothing, and its report formatters are long runs of
# `writeln!(...)?` whose `nexits` counts say nothing about production
# maintainability.
./big-code-analysis-bench/**
./generate-grammars/**
./man/**
./abuild-keys/**
./**/examples/**
./check-*.py
./verify-*.py
